# Copy to .env.local. Never commit .env.local.

# Where the FastAPI backend lives. Must match one of the origins apps/api
# allows (see WEB_ORIGIN in the repo-root .env.example) or the browser will
# refuse the response before this app ever sees it.
#
# IN PRODUCTION THIS MUST BE https://. The page is served over HTTPS, so an
# http:// value makes every API call mixed content, which Safari blocks
# outright — and the symptom is an app that installs to the home screen and
# then loads nothing. It is also inlined at BUILD time, so changing it on
# Vercel requires a redeploy, not just a restart.
#
# **REQUIRED FOR A PRODUCTION BUILD SINCE W6.** `pnpm build` runs
# `scripts/check-env.mjs` first and exits non-zero when this is missing, empty,
# or not scheme-qualified. That closes known issue #80: an *unset* value took the
# localhost fallback but an **empty** one did not, so every request went to a
# relative path the deployment does not serve and the error read "Could not reach
# the API at ." — indistinguishable from the API being down. Vercel lets you save
# an empty string, so it was reachable. `pnpm dev` is unaffected.
#
# Production: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.foundgrant.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
